 # Futureox Design development
+
+- The 2026-10-26 large-file edit continuation is recorded in [its paired GUI evidence](../../../testing/verification-large-edit-20261026/README.md). Released initial interaction captures yield to exact repair; unchanged edit viewports avoid a redundant coarse pass without certifying stale content. Complete native workset replacements use actual full synchronization to establish their source receipt, avoiding repeated 52 MB interaction copies; partial edits remain incremental and receipt/CAS guards are unchanged. Three topology worksets improved, but the largest measured stop-to-refinement interval remains about 6.7 seconds. The maintenance-cohort and translated-source experiments were not adopted after real measurements; do not reintroduce them from isolated tests.
 
 - The 2026-10-26 motion-continuity repair is recorded in [its evidence and remaining failures](../../../testing/verification-motion-continuity-20261025/README.md). Atomic layer import, exact background initialization, scoped cancellation and resource admission address reproduced transparency failures; retained-frame quality alone cannot establish timely object motion. The wide rational prefix candidate remains strictly opt-in. Real fast zoom and topology edit convergence still fail; do not call this a complete rendering fix.
 
